    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        0,
        760
      ],
      "size": [
        1440,
        300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX 3 Image Klein + PiD, tuned for a 12 GB Arc B580\n\nType a short request in **Prompt**. The prompt upsampler expands it into the full scene caption Klein needs (BFL: never run Klein without one). The caption is shown in **Caption sent to the model**; turn **Use prompt upsampler** off to send your own caption verbatim.\n\nKlein (distilled, 15 steps, cfg 1) renders at about 1 MP, then PiD decodes that latent straight into a 4x image (1 MP in, 16 MP out) in 4 steps. The upsampler has a fixed seed, so rerolling the image seed reuses the cached caption and skips the LLM.\n\n### Files (under `/data/models/`)\n\n| Folder | File | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| diffusion_models | flux3-image-klein-int8-convrot.safetensors | 5.8 GB |\n| text_encoders | qwen3vl_4b_int8_convrot.safetensors | 4.9 GB |\n| text_encoders | qwen3.5_9b_flux3_prompt_upsampler_w4a8.safetensors | 6.7 GB |\n| vae | flux2-vae.safetensors | 0.3 GB |\n| diffusion_models | pid_1.5_flux2_1024_to_4096_4step_bf16.safetensors | 2.8 GB |\n| text_encoders | gemma_2_2b_it_elm_fp8_scaled.safetensors | 2.6 GB |\n\nThe first four come from [black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein-comfy](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein-comfy) (gated: accept the license first), the last two from [Comfy-Org/PixelDiT](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/PixelDiT).\n\n### Knobs\n- Aspect ratio: any preset in **Base resolution**; keep megapixels near 1.0, PiD is trained on 1024 px inputs.\n- Every file is sized to load completely on 12 GB. The bf16 Klein (11.1 GB) and the int8 upsampler (9.8 GB) would load only partially, which on Arc tends to end in `UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_RESOURCES`.\n- PiD out of memory: `pid_flux2_512_to_2048_4step_bf16` with megapixels 0.25 gives 2K instead of 4K.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
